    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Established on the `cas-certificate` route. The gap this closes was named by the lane that opened the domain as the sharpest limit of its work: its base-case checker only evaluated at concrete integers, so every multi-parameter identity stopped at its recurrence. The new axiom `cas.symbolic-gamma-arguments-avoid-poles` is the honest price -- an uncancelled symbolic Gamma power is treated as nonzero and finite, which for integer parameters holds away from the non-positive integers. Here every symbolic Gamma cancels, so the assumption bites only on the arguments' definedness, not on their values.",
